{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea","id":1360932,"title":"Looking for help to make Fetch splats for a Chronicle idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-14T12:58:46-08:00","id":1360932,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Looking for help to make Fetch splats for a Chronicle idea","content":"So I'm planning a Chronicle where the PCs are playing Fetches whose lives are disrupted by their originals returning to the world...sort of the reverse of your typical situation. The plan is to let the players start with the Enter The Hedge and Mimic Contract Echoes, since that will give the players access to a lot of the same things a normal Changeling game would have access to.<br /> <br /> But I also want to introduce some character splat to allow the PCs some more options. I'm considering allowing some Promethean Bestowments, based on what a particular character is made out of, but would like suggestions for Bestowment ideas that would fit with Fetches, since some of the Promethean Bestowments are pretty specific.<br /> <br /> I'm aiming for 4 &quot;splats&quot;, based on the categories of ingredients from the 1e Autumn Nightmares book: Man-Made Materials, Natural Materials, Flesh, and Fae-Stuff. If anyone has an idea for a 5th sort of ingredient (to match with the typical CoD method of having 5+ basic splats to choose from), I'm interested in hearing those ideas as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T06:17:08-08:00","id":1361449,"title":"","content":"Fetches are but bundles of discarded dreams and shadows.<br /> <br /> Splats the Four Bundles<br /> <br /> The Bundle of Cloth and Clay<br /> AKA Reflections, Mirrors, Cast offs<br /> Made from the cast of refuse of the world of men these Fetches can adapt and hide amidst the throng of humanity, adaptability and longing define them. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Bundle of Sticks and Stones<br /> AKA Echoes, Effigies, Scarecrows<br /> Made from the world around mortals but not of mortals these fetches draw upon endurance and eternity of the simplest and first things. Fortitude and aloofness are their hallmarks.<br /> <br /> The Bundle of Blood and Bones<br /> AKA Dopplegangers, Twins, Clones<br /> Closest to the mortals and their passions these fetches are imbued with their passions and instinct. The blood of man drenches them with vigor and stains them with fury.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Bundle of Aughts and Ends<br /> AKA Moonlit Shadow, Silver Dreams, Memories<br /> <br /> These fetches are made from that which is not of the world of mortal man and seem to drift as ghosts or remembered as memories seeming to call upon happenstance to guide them. They are matched with fate while forever eerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T06:24:49-08:00","id":1361450,"title":"","content":"The Bundle of Naught and Nothing<br /> AKA the Forgotten, the Unwanted, Them<br /> <br /> <br /> Those who are emptiest and without purpose sometimes fetches seem to appear manifested by the absence of the stolen man. They are unbound by the whims of the Gentry and were unnamed remanents who found their way into the mortal world through the hole left in the stolen\u2019s wake. Unknown defined by being unseen and forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:46:15-08:00","id":1361591,"title":"","content":"All of these are really cool, and exactly what I'm going for.<br /> <br /> But tell me more about this last one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1361450#post1361450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bundle of Naught and Nothing<br /> AKA the Forgotten, the Unwanted, Them<br /> <br /> <br /> Those who are emptiest and without purpose sometimes fetches seem to appear manifested by the absence of the stolen man. They are unbound by the whims of the Gentry and were unnamed remanents who found their way into the mortal world through the hole left in the stolen\u2019s wake. Unknown defined by being unseen and forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this suggesting that there are some Fetches who just appear out of nowhere? Why do they appear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T16:57:38-08:00","id":1361608,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah I made them up for this thread. The idea being sometimes the Gentry don\u2019t make Fetches when they spirit away mortals. But later these mortals return as Changeling and still find fetches. Who made them? Maybe they appeared on their own? Perhaps on the other side of Oblivion when you lose your true name you drown in that endless sea of disparity where swims the Primordial Leviathan, but for some unknown reason some may notice on the other end of the coin that is existence in this Briney Oblivion trails that lead them back. Metaphysically filling the vacuum left by the mortal, and maybe the Wyrd abhors a vaccuum. What were these beings before becoming a fetch? They don\u2019t know. Why did they find themselves in the stolen lives of another? Who knows, perhaps losing their true name and drowning in disparity which lies beyond death itself they were in lives much like the stolen mortals. Maybe their lost names shared similar Supernal syllables. Pherhaps even they not only experienced a resonant but different life, they also experienced it on a resonant but different worlds? Perhaps somewhere out there someone lies about not knowing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T15:59:46-08:00","id":1362006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1361608#post1361608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah I made them up for this thread. The idea being sometimes the Gentry don\u2019t make Fetches when they spirit away mortals. But later these mortals return as Changeling and still find fetches. Who made them? Maybe they appeared on their own? Perhaps on the other side of Oblivion when you lose your true name you drown in that endless sea of disparity where swims the Primordial Leviathan, but for some unknown reason some may notice on the other end of the coin that is existence in this Briney Oblivion trails that lead them back. Metaphysically filling the vacuum left by the mortal, and maybe the Wyrd abhors a vaccuum. What were these beings before becoming a fetch? They don\u2019t know. Why did they find themselves in the stolen lives of another? Who knows, perhaps losing their true name and drowning in disparity which lies beyond death itself they were in lives much like the stolen mortals. Maybe their lost names shared similar Supernal syllables. Pherhaps even they not only experienced a resonant but different life, they also experienced it on a resonant but different worlds? Perhaps somewhere out there someone lies about not knowing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I very much like this idea of <i>ex nihilo</i> Fetches. However, I don't think I can offer it as a PC splat, since this particular game is focused around a group of Fetches made by the same creator banding together for protection against their counterparts. Themes of rage against their creator and the desire to become fully human (both things I'm planning to import from Promethean, to the point of offering Prometheans as an option for characters to pursue) are going to be important, and these <i>ex nihilo</i> fetches don't really fit with it. I'll probably use this idea for NPCs, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T16:41:15-08:00","id":1362018,"title":"","content":"Perhaps though the creator of the others took the human that this fetch is the fetch of, and everyone including the fetch assumes that Gentry created it?<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of mixing this with Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T09:57:16-08:00","id":1362143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1362018#post1362018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps though the creator of the others took the human that this fetch is the fetch of, and everyone including the fetch assumes that Gentry created it?<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of mixing this with Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This particular Fae is more interested in crafting fetches than having servants -- he takes people specifically so he can show off his skill at crafting replacements for them, and he sells the people he steals to other Gentry. It's the same reason he'd act as a Demiurge for a Promethean -- he's trying to prove that his creations are &quot;better than real people&quot; to fulfill an oath and satisfy an Aspiration, and he's perfectly willing to murder someone and craft a Promethean out of their remains to make his point (he might not be <i>capable</i> of wielding the Divine Fire more than once, but he's certainly <i>willing</i> to give it a go).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:04:30-08:00","id":1362862,"title":"","content":"What less 'material', but not purely fae?<br /> <br /> The sunlight that was peering through the window, the readily available cold of the winter day when they were stolen, the electricity that was pulsing through the wires, the chatter from the TV, the very screams the victim emitted when the True Fae unveiled their true form. Not quite energy itself, because the nature of them is part of how its crafted. Electricity from a wall circuit is different from lightning, laughter different from screams. The material type is best described as 'Ephemeral'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T01:11:50-08:00","id":1363037,"title":"","content":"Here's what I have so far, based on the ideas from this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham, serif\">Ingredient </span><span style=\"font-family:Rackham, serif\">Bundles</span></span></span><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Gentry can craft a fetch in mere moments, using whatever is handy, binding a scrap of their target\u2019s shadow and a few drops of their blood with convenient detritus twisted into a human form. Fetches might wind up created out of manmade material (garbage, clothes, objects from a victim\u2019s home); natural material (leaves, sticks, dirt); living or once-living material (the victim\u2019s pets, animals plucked from the surrounding area); or fae-stuff the Fair One has with it (the cloak off their back, candles burned out during the hunt, arrows used to pin a target\u2019s shadow to the ground). Others can also take their time, putting effort into the fetch of their target. A Fetch might wind up being made of an ice sculpture, a porcelain doll, a wicker effigy, or their own clothing stuffed with leaves and topped with the head of a pi<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style\">\u00f1</span>ata.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">In the end, it doesn\u2019t make much difference \u2013 the Fae\u2019s magic is what animates the Fetch,</span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"> gives it the semblance of life and allows the fetch to mimic nearly any human behavior. The skill that the Fae employs when crafting the fetch is what makes the difference. The </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">fetch behaves only as human-like as it was crafted to behave. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">But a Fetch\u2019s construction does have an impact on their personality, as well as the sorts of Echoes they develop. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">A fetch made of the clothes of the person it\u2019s impersonating might be better able to carry off the charade in superficial ways, but be incapable of real empathy; it is, in effect, an empty suit. A fetch made from fae-stuff might show more of an affinity for faerie magic and the Hedge, while one made from dead animals might become feral </span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">and impulsive over time.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Over time, various Autumn Courts have attempted to classify Fetches by their construction and behavior, </span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">the better to understand the Gentry. The following classifications are the results of such research (not done for the Fetch\u2019s benefit, of course, which is why they have so many unflattering nicknames). </span></span></div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mannequins</span></b></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of Cloth and Porcelain</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA Cast-Offs, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Poppets</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, Mummers</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">We are what we pretend to be, so we must be very careful what we pretend to be.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Kurt Vonnegut, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>Mother Night</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Gentry are fascinated with human ingenuity and materials, and might opt to fashion their Fetches partially or entirely out of human-made objects that catch their eye for whatever reason. One might take a plastic doll out of the crib of their target\u2019s child and dress it up. Another might tear open their victim\u2019s computer and build a figurine out of wires and motherboards. Yet another might use a kitschy heart-shaped watch, a deck of playing cards, and the cups in the cupboard. And another might hand-carve a life-sized marionette with their target\u2019s likeness </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">out of wood stolen from their couch</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mannequins made this way have a good understanding of the human world, though depending on what they\u2019re made from this might be genuine empathy or shallow manipulation. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Either way, mannequins are good at \u201cfaking it,\u201d showing reactions that people around them expect to see while keeping their true feelings buried.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effigies</span></b></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of Sticks and Stones</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mockeries, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Piles, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Scarecrows</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">We are the hollow men</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">We are the stuffed men</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Leaning together</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Headpiece filled with straw. Alas!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Our dried voices, when</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">We whisper together</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Are quiet and meaningless</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">As wind in dry grass</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Or rats' feet over broken glass</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">In our dry cellar\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">T.S. Eliot, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>The Hollow Men</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The stereotypical image most Changelings have of the Fetch is that they\u2019re hastily made piles of whatever objects are within arms reach \u2013 twigs, leaves, clods of dirt, pebbles, string, ash, and so on. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Gentry</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> fashion these </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">piles</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> into rough approximations of a human form. One might stuff straw into the person\u2019s clothes and top it with a carved pumpkin for a head. Another might craft a figure out of sticks and river mud. Yet another might use a stapler to </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">hold together a crude figurine of soup cans. And another might dump out a trash can and fashion a figurine out of banana peels, discarded spaghetti, and coffee grounds. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Natural components are always at hand, hold memories well, and the effigies produced tend to be obedient and level-headed (at least at first), making for good duplicate of their human \u201cbase.\u201d At least, they do if the Gentry is skilled enough to create a good likeness. If the Fae isn\u2019t so skilled, an effigy might be gruff, moody, and hard to read.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Replicants</b></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of Flesh and Bones</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Zombies, Ferals, Clones</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">I want more </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>life</i></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, fucker.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Roy Batty, Blade Runner</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Others aren\u2019t limited to inorganic materials, or even unliving ones, when crafting a Fetch. Any material that was once part of an animal (or a human) can be incorporated into the Fetch, and some Others revel in the bloody, messy business. One might tear off a pound of flesh from a person dying at the scene of a car crash as the price for saving their life. Another might carry a pocketful of dried bones, fangs, and teeth </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">to use in case the fancy strikes them. Yet another might slaughter the family dog just for the occasion. And another might weave a glamour on a passing raccoon, a reverse of the process that turns Man to Beast. These replicants are imbued with passions and instinct, drenching them with vigor and staining them with fury. Replicants are closest to feeling real, human emotion (instead of faking it like a mannequin), but aren\u2019t any closer to actual empathy, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">instead making them impulsive and mercurial.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mirages</span></b></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Shade</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> and </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mirrors</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Spooks</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Reflections</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Daydreams</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">We are such stuff</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">As dreams are made on, and our little life</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Is rounded with a sleep.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prospero, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>The Tempest</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">To the Others, metaphor is as good as </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">truth</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Some of the Others are skilled enough to pull the ephemeral into the physical to serve as Fetches. One might use the entire shadow instead of just a scrap. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">A</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">nother might weave smoke, wind, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">and lightning</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> together into a human form. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Yet</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> other might reach into a mirror and pull </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">forth the person\u2019s reflection. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">And one might reach into the person\u2019s own dreams and fashion a Fetch from their memories and subconscious feelings. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">These mirages tend to be quite a bit more \u201coff\u201d from their base than most Fetches \u2013 either they focus on </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">one aspect of their base\u2019s personality, exaggerating it until it completely consumes them, or else they act very different from their base, like a mirror reflection of their previous values and personality.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Curios</span></b></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Odds</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> and </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Ends</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Knickknacks, Trash Pandas, Cuckoos</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Six is having problems</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Adjusting to his clone status</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Have to put him on a shelf</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">All day long we hear him crying so loud</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I just wanna be myself</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I just wanna be myself</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I just wanna be myself</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Be myself</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Be myself\u201d</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Alice Cooper, </span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Clones (We\u2019re All)</span></i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">There is, of course, nothing stopping The Others from combining disparate elements </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">into a Fetch. It\u2019s not even particularly uncommon. One might weave a Fetch from cobwebs, bathroom tissue, a live slug, and an ERECTOR Set. Another might use the color of dreams as makeup on a broken Barbie doll, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">and replace its </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">missing limbs with sticks. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Yet another might fill their victim\u2019s pet cat with 10,000 volts then dress the corpse up with silverware from their kitchen. And one might pull up a log from a peat bog, carve a likeness into it, and then char it the right color with a Zippo lighter. The Fae aren\u2019t picky when it comes to ingredients, and curios are very much mixed bags, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">which is probably why most act at least slightly eccentric. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Curios tend to develop strange habits and fixations over time, and many seem somewhat disconnected from reality.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Doppelgangers</span></b></span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Bundles of Aughts and Ends</span></span></span></b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">AKA </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Nemeses,</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Masks, Quislings</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">That ain't me, that ain't my face. It wasn't even me when I was trying to be that face. I wasn't even really me the</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">n</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">; I was just being the way I looked, the way people wanted.\u201d</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2013</span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Chief Bromden, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>One Flew Over The Cuckoo\u2019s Nest</i></span></span></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Others often bring stuff with them from Arcadia when they hunt, and sometimes, when they desire a more direct eyes in the mortal world, they\u2019ll used these glamour-infused objects in the construction of their Fetches. One might use scraps from their own cloak, burned out candles used to light the way through the Briers, and snapped shafts from arrows used to pin a target\u2019s shadow to the ground. Another might transform a hobgoblin servant into their target\u2019s likeness, tearing out their heart and fixing a piece of the human\u2019s shadow in its place much like they do with a Huntsman. Yet another might enchant a piece of their jewelery, claiming it to be \u201can equitable exchange\u201d before the Wyrd. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">And one might simply command a Fetch to appear </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><i>ex nihilo</i></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> from the void created by their target\u2019s absence. These doppelgangers are almost always aware of their true roles and origins, and receive explicit commands from The Gentry over and above simply being placeholders. Once the Gentry have departed with their prize, though, the doppelganger is left to its own devices. Many resent being told who they are \u201csupposed\u201d to be, and this resentment can cause them to lash out. Some take out their frustrations on their adopted families, playing the part of Evil Twin. Others make radical breaks with their base\u2019s relatives and loved ones and attempt to divorce themselves from the role they were dropped in in order to find their true selves.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T14:57:31-08:00","id":1363516,"title":"","content":"So with some splats in place, I'm going to work on converting Echoes. It makes sense to me to format these like they've been formatting supernatrual powers in the 2e books, so here's my take on an Echo that didn't make it into the initial 2e book:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Rackham\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Feast of Shadows </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The fetch can consume the shadows of living beings in order to heal themselves. They must either touch their target or their target\u2019s shadow to use this power. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Wyrd 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Cost</b>: 1 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dice Pool</b>: Dexterity + Wits + Wyrd vs. target\u2019s Resolve + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Action</b>: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Duration</b>: The shadow begins at the same Size as the person who casts it, plus the target\u2019s Supernatural Tolerance (if any). It loses 1 Size each turn whether it\u2019s being eaten or not, and vanishes when it reaches Size 0.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Roll Results</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Success</b>: The Fetch captures the target\u2019s shadow and tears it away. The victim loses a point of Willpower and gains the Spooked Condition from the shock. The shadow regenerates itself within one scene, or sooner if the victim regains Willpower before the current Scene ends. This power can only steal shadows from living beings with souls. Constructed beings like Prometheans or the Fetch themselves and undead such as Vampires are immune to this power.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Once the Fetch has captured the shadow, they can spend an instant action each turn to consume it as long as it lasts. While consuming it, the Fetch heals damage; the Fetch heals one level of bashing damage per turn spent eating the shadow, one point of lethal damage for every two turns and one point of aggravated damage for every three turns. The Fetch can choose what order to heal this damage in, if applicable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>For example, a Fetch battles their changeling and does poorly, suffering three points of bashing damage and one lethal. Fleeing, the Fetch finds a man waiting at a bus stop and rips his shadow away. The man is Size 5, so the shadow begins at Size 5 as well. It takes the Fetch one turn to get to an alleyway to eat in peace (Size 4). The Fetch spends two turns eating the shadow and heals one level of lethal damage (Size 2). A drunk man stumbles into the alley and vomits into a trash can; the Fetch is startled and stops eating, and the shadow fades a bit more (Size 1). Annoyed, the Fetch finishes the shadow (healing one level of bashing damage), and stalks after the drunk who distracted him to tear his shadow away.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The shadow\u2019s effective size is doubled, and the victim gains the Frightened Condition instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Failure</b>: The Fetch\u2019s hands go straight through the shadow without effect. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The Fetch accidentally tears off their own shadow, which disintegrates in their hand. The Fetch loses a point of Willpower and gains the Frightened Condition. The shadow regenerates after a scene, as above.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Mirage</b>: The Spook adds 3 to the shadow\u2019s effective size, and the shadow does not begin shrinking for 2 rounds after it is torn off.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Doppelganger</b>: The Nemesis deals a point of bashing damage to the target, in addition to the other effects, or lethal if they got an Exceptional Success. If the Nemesis is tearing off the shadow of their Changeling counterpart, this damage is upgraded to lethal and aggravated, respectively. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T01:47:24-08:00","id":1364497,"title":"","content":"Question for the community:<br /> <br /> Fetches are created in part by taking a piece of the Changeling donor's shadow to serve as the basis for their personality and memories, which is often thought of as a metaphor for the soul. Am I off base in considering this an Icon? And, if it so, what sorts of in-game effects might it have for the Fetch? Would it be something like a Needle or Thread that they could draw Willpower from? Or would it be more like a Touchstone that they refer back to when facing a breaking point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T08:26:24-08:00","id":1364543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364497#post1364497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the community:<br /> <br /> Fetches are created in part by taking a piece of the Changeling donor's shadow to serve as the basis for their personality and memories, which is often thought of as a metaphor for the soul. Am I off base in considering this an Icon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Icons are formed from a changeling's escape from Faerie as a consequence of their passing through the Thorns \u2014 they come too late in the game to be part of any fetch that wasn't made well after the durance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T10:07:02-08:00","id":1364557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364543#post1364543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Icons are formed from a changeling's escape from Faerie as a consequence of their passing through the Thorns \u2014 they come too late in the game to be part of any fetch that wasn't made well after the durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a change from 1e? Because I remember it being the initial passage into the Thorns that did the damage, and passing back allowed them to reclaim some of the bits they lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T13:37:10-08:00","id":1364598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364557#post1364557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a change from 1e? Because I remember it being the initial passage into the Thorns that did the damage, and passing back allowed them to reclaim some of the bits they lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Icons weren't a thing in 1e and they're connected to the point at which changelings have Clarity, which didn't happen immediately in 1e either -- 1e fae-touched (with Morality instead of Clarity) were the result of leaving before the full changeling template settled in and as a result any fetch that was left in their place disintegrated when they escaped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:02:52-08:00","id":1364628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364598#post1364598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Icons weren't a thing in 1e and they're connected to the point at which changelings have Clarity, which didn't happen immediately in 1e either -- 1e fae-touched (with Morality instead of Clarity) were the result of leaving before the full changeling template settled in and as a result any fetch that was left in their place disintegrated when they escaped.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm.<br /> <br /> So my next question then becomes...is there anything especially <i>wrong</i> with the idea of the Piece of Shadow functioning like an Icon? Even if it isn't strictly tied to the changeling's escape, it's still an intimate piece of the changeling that was stripped away. It becomes a tangible Thing that a changeling Might Want Back, giving them a reason to come into conflict with their Fetch over and above raging at their Keepers or disgust with how their life has been lived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:21:13-08:00","id":1364634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364628#post1364628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my next question then becomes...is there anything especially <i>wrong</i> with the idea of the Piece of Shadow functioning like an Icon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The big thing? Icons are found in the Hedge, and cease to exist when removed from the Hedge by the right person. Many fetches can't even <i>enter</i> the Hedge, and most are ostensibly completed well outside the Thorns, and while temporal weirdness is always on the table when it comes to the fae, it feels a bit egregious to have the thing that's bound to changelings' shadows being shaped funny consistently break the order of events in this manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if it isn't strictly tied to the changeling's escape, it's still an intimate piece of the changeling that was stripped away. It becomes a tangible Thing that a changeling Might Want Back, giving them a reason to come into conflict with their Fetch over and above raging at their Keepers or disgust with how their life has been lived. </div> </div> </div>I feel like 1e presented plenty of alternatives that made destroying your fetch a desirable outcome, most prominently specialized Merits to represent particular sorts of boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T18:05:38-08:00","id":1364656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364634#post1364634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big thing? Icons are found in the Hedge, and cease to exist when removed from the Hedge by the right person. Many fetches can't even <i>enter</i> the Hedge, and most are ostensibly completed well outside the Thorns</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does that matter? People who are <i>not </i>the right person can bring Icons out of the Hedge without them vanishing. &quot;An enemy has my Icon&quot; and &quot;I know where an Icon of yours got to&quot; seem to be the intrinsic story beats tied to their existence, not the fact that you can trek through the Hedge to discover them. Icons are MacGuffins. They're plot devices. They exist as a Desirable Thing To Get and Something That Must Be Kept Out Of The Wrong Hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while temporal weirdness is always on the table when it comes to the fae, it feels a bit egregious to have the thing that's bound to changelings' shadows being shaped funny consistently break the order of events in this manner. </div> </div> </div>I feel like we may have a difference of opinion when it comes to when, exactly, a person starts being transformed into a Changeling. The creation of a Fetch is the second major act of malice that The Others perform on a person (the first act, or course, being the decision to kidnap them in the first place) and the first act that involves actual violation of them on a spiritual level. Fetches don't happen by accident (unless I decide to use that <i>ex nihilo</i> fetch idea someone pitched earlier in the thread). If, perhaps, a person was to escape the clutches of their would-be Keeper somehow and make their way through the Thorns back Ironsides without ever seeing Arcadia, the Fetch would still be there (unless they disintegrate like you mention 1e Fetches did...what book is that in?).<br /> <br /> And even if the Fetch <i>does</i> disintegrate...what happens to that piece of shadow/soul? Does it just automatically return to the lucky escapee? Does it also disintegrate, leaving the person it was taken from with a void for the rest of their lives? Or is it still there, fluttering in the wreckage, waiting to be picked up by someone? That, I feel, is the importance of an Icon, not the fact that the rest of them are created in the Hedge, nor when the rest of them are created (coming <i>or</i> going).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like 1e presented plenty of alternatives that made destroying your fetch a desirable outcome, most prominently specialized Merits to represent particular sorts of boons. </div> </div> </div>None of those Merits especially motivated the Fetch themselves to fight back, though. Keeping the one piece of soul they have does.<br /> <br /> The whole idea of making PC-playable Fetch is to explore what it means to be something that thought they were human but learned they weren't. It's playing with the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CloningBlues\" target=\"_blank\">Cloning Blues</a>, <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TomatoInTheMirror\" target=\"_blank\">Tomato in the Mirror</a>, and <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AndroidsArePeopleToo\" target=\"_blank\">Androids Are People Too</a>/<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClonesArePeopleToo\" target=\"_blank\">Clones Are People Too</a> tropes (fair warning, all TVTropes links). Every piece of C:tL fiction I've seen where Fetch are involved treat them as disposable, of lesser importance than the Changeling they were made from, or imply that the Changeling is morally justified destroying them to get their life back. That's kind of fucked up when you think about it hard enough. Even in the Anthology stories, all the ones with Fetch in them <i>end</i> with the discovery that one is a Fetch...when that's really just the beginning. The Fetch now has to try to live with and cope with the knowledge of what they are -- all the while dealing with a being who doesn't believe they have the right to <i>exist</i>.<br /> <br /> I've heard Promethean described as being an allegory for the queer experience (trying to exist in a world where you know you're different from almost everyone else, and where those difference make people hate you just for existing), and Changeling itself is very much a survivor allegory (a person who has suffered unimaginable trauma now has to pick up the pieces of their life and move on somehow). Well, what I think this particular rabbit hole I've tumbled into is a neurodivergence allegory -- coming to the realization that you <i>aren't</i> like everyone else, there is a reason why, it's tied into the very fabric of your being, and now you have to cope with that knowledge, all while others don't understand or they <i>think</i> they do, and think of you as an inferior version of a person (if they think of you as a person at all, and not just an object to be dealt with).<br /> <br /> Right. That was a tangent and a half. Let me tie it back to the Shadow-as-Icon idea. The Shadow is a metaphor for a lot of things, and to the Gentry, a metaphor is as good as truth. How I'm seeing this is that when they take a piece of the abductee's shadow, it's coming from the Jungian Archetype just as much as the physical darkness or metaphysical soul. They're taking a piece of that bit of us we all hide, that least desirable bit of someone (a guilt, a shame, an anxiety, an insecurity, etc.) to use as the seed that anchors their construct's personality in place, that makes it able to impersonate the person they're abducting. Calling it an Icon means that, as per the description, this Shadow is a memory, probably one with a specific emotion attached to it, in physical form. The Changeling has reason to want it back (it improves their Clarity, the way that confronting your Shadow self and embodying it supposedly helps you become a more rounded person), other Changelings might want it (to use as leverage or vengeance, not caring about all this soul/Id crap), but it's also forming the very basis of the Fetch's entire existence. The Fetch literally cannot exist without it. So it creates a conflict, which is what drama (and thus, Storytelling) is all about. And it does this in a way that a Changeling gaining a Merit from breaking their Fetch <i>doesn't</i>. Sure, it's an Icon that's not in the Hedge. It's an Icon that was created even before the Changeling was altered enough to be considered a changeling. It's an Icon that's easily accessible -- all it requires is the murder of another sentient being, one that quite literally is a part of yourself.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's not <i>literally</i> an Icon. But having it have all the characteristics of one opens up story opportunities, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T18:23:01-08:00","id":1364659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364656#post1364656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that matter? People who are <i>not </i>the right person can bring Icons out of the Hedge without them vanishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the people in a position to get ahold of an Icon are disinclined to leave the Hedge, the right person needs to <i>bring the Icon out of the Hedge</i> to integrate it, and at the time of this conversation we have no data on whether the wrong person <i>can</i> take an Icon out of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;An enemy has my Icon&quot; and &quot;I know where an Icon of yours got to&quot; seem to be the intrinsic story beats tied to their existence, not the fact that you can trek through the Hedge to discover them. Icons are MacGuffins. They're plot devices. They exist as a Desirable Thing To Get and Something That Must Be Kept Out Of The Wrong Hands. </div> </div> </div>They are not the only things with this quality and they have specific qualities that relate to a specific order of events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like we may have a difference of opinion when it comes to when, exactly, a person starts being transformed into a Changeling. </div> </div> </div>It is a thing that happens in Arcadia. That is the metaphysics of the thing. It is specifically something the Fae cannot manage outside of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If, perhaps, a person was to escape the clutches of their would-be Keeper somehow and make their way through the Thorns back Ironsides without ever seeing Arcadia, the Fetch would still be there (unless they disintegrate like you mention 1e Fetches did...what book is that in?). </div> </div> </div>Equinox Road has an entire sidebar on the topic on page 105, where the section on the process of becoming a changeling is discussed. &quot;Only actual changelings must deal with the trauma of having a fetch.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even if the Fetch <i>does</i> disintegrate...what happens to that piece of shadow/soul? Does it just automatically return to the lucky escapee? Does it also disintegrate, leaving the person it was taken from with a void for the rest of their lives? Or is it still there, fluttering in the wreckage, waiting to be picked up by someone? That, I feel, is the importance of an Icon, not the fact that the rest of them are created in the Hedge, nor when the rest of them are created (coming <i>or</i> going). </div> </div> </div>&quot;When [the fetch] vanishes, the mortal automatically gains back the fragment of her soul or shadow that it contained, along with the general memories of what occurred in her absence.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shadow is a metaphor for a lot of things, and to the Gentry, a metaphor is as good as truth. </div> </div> </div>The shadow the fae deal with is more consistently tied to the shadow-as-soul-anatomy concept found in other games, where your shadow is your image, reflection, echo, and other secondhand impact upon the world. The fae give your fetch a piece of your shadow because that's a stand-in for giving it your place in reality. Some of them inform hidden shames that bear confronting, but in general the point of reference for fetches is &quot;the changeling, with a notable difference,&quot; or sometimes &quot;the changeling, proceeding as they were before they became a changeling.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fetches as playable characters have far more cause to draw upon their traumatized existential bases for the Jungian reading of the shadow, and frankly in a game where you're playing as the doppelganger holding someone's place in the world there's no actual need to determine if the thing giving you animation will give them Clarity or give other people knowledge of them \u2014 you have an intrinsic connection to their dreams and get more magically potent whenever they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-01-2020, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:04:23-08:00","id":1364683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364659#post1364659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the people in a position to get ahold of an Icon are disinclined to leave the Hedge, the right person needs to <i>bring the Icon out of the Hedge</i> to integrate it, and at the time of this conversation we have no data on whether the wrong person <i>can</i> take an Icon out of the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair Enough. I remember the MacGuffin in the demo being an Icon (well, that and the guy who betrayed the motley), but TBF it was the Goblin Queen who had it, and she didn't take it <i>with</i> her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is a thing that happens in Arcadia. That is the metaphysics of the thing. It is specifically something the Fae cannot manage outside of Arcadia. </div> </div> </div>Hmm. This is <i>also</i> something I'd disagree on, but I admit that that's moving into House Rule territory, so fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Equinox Road has an entire sidebar on the topic on page 105, where the section on the process of becoming a changeling is discussed. &quot;Only actual changelings must deal with the trauma of having a fetch.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When [the fetch] vanishes, the mortal automatically gains back the fragment of her soul or shadow that it contained, along with the general memories of what occurred in her absence.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are not the only things with this quality and they have specific qualities that relate to a specific order of events. </div> </div> </div>Alrighty. Time to read Equinox Road again...it's been a while.<br /> <br /> So &quot;As long as the person rescued is not yet transformed into a changeling, the binding that holds their fetch together is not yet completely stable.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Icons don't form until the changeling escapes Arcadia, is it enough to say that the Shadow represents this binding? That it &quot;becomes&quot; an Icon once the changeling has left the Thorns, and didn't have all the properties of an Icon until that moment? That might also serve as the mechanism for Fetch to realize their double has returned...something fundamental in their Shadow &quot;solidified&quot; right then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fetches as playable characters have far more cause to draw upon their traumatized existential bases for the Jungian reading of the shadow, and frankly in a game where you're playing as the doppelganger holding someone's place in the world there's no actual need to determine if the thing giving you animation will give them Clarity or give other people knowledge of them \u2014 you have an intrinsic connection to their dreams and get more magically potent whenever they do. </div> </div> </div>Promethean goes into great detail about what Centimani and Alchemists do with the Vitriol they steal from captive Created. It informs why the conflict between them exists. Centemani (at least in 2e) can't progress on their own Pilgrimages, so can't generate Vitrol on their own and thus need to steal it to get more power, while alchemists use it for all sorts of stuff, such as permanently turning lead into gold, slowing down aging, or going all Transhuman Nightmare with Dread Powers. They don't give us charts for how much Vitriol one needs to turn lead into gold, sure, but we get the broad strokes.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to hit a few marks with this mechanic:<br /> <br /> 1) The Shadow is something that the Fetch has that both the changeling they are bound to wants, and that other changelings might have a reason to want.<br /> 2) The Shadow represents a part of the Fetch's personality in some fashion, along with (or maybe in place of) their Needle and Thread. I still don't know if i want to make it a Willpower mechanic, a mechanic tied to a Fetch's Integrity, or some other function.<br /> 3) I want to have a villain in this game who is mainly a threat to Fetches other than his own because he wants to collect Fetch Shadows for Reasons.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing any reason the Shadow can't function like an Icon. Why does the timing of Icon creation and icons mostly being in the Hedge matter? What is the actual issue, other than fluff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:48:15-08:00","id":1364691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364683#post1364683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might also serve as the mechanism for Fetch to realize their double has returned...something fundamental in their Shadow &quot;solidified&quot; right then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, a fetch realizes something is amiss when they start being able to see through the Mask, which coincides with the person whose shadow they have escaping Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethean goes into great detail about what Centimani and Alchemists do with the Vitriol they steal from captive Created. It informs why the conflict between them exists. Centemani (at least in 2e) can't progress on their own Pilgrimages, so can't generate Vitrol on their own and thus need to steal it to get more power, while alchemists use it for all sorts of stuff, such as permanently turning lead into gold, slowing down aging, or going all Transhuman Nightmare with Dread Powers. They don't give us charts for how much Vitriol one needs to turn lead into gold, sure, but we get the broad strokes. </div> </div> </div>Promethean is a game where character advancement is dependent upon Vitriol and hanging onto it in an unspent form is a risk balanced by the drawbacks of raising Azoth. It is a game where the volatility of your occult nature and your lack of a normal human background are things that give you cause to struggle with the question of humanity in a different manner to the placeholder for a person who was, in many cases, literally stolen from their life. The reasons a changeling has for seeking the destruction of their fetch are personal and typically have little to do with the wisps of magic giving it thought and motion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm trying to hit a few marks with this mechanic:<br /> <br /> 1) The Shadow is something that the Fetch has that both the changeling they are bound to wants, and that other changelings might have a reason to want.<br /> 2) The Shadow represents a part of the Fetch's personality in some fashion, along with (or maybe in place of) their Needle and Thread. I still don't know if i want to make it a Willpower mechanic, a mechanic tied to a Fetch's Integrity, or some other function.<br /> 3) I want to have a villain in this game who is mainly a threat to Fetches other than his own because he wants to collect Fetch Shadows for Reasons.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing any reason the Shadow can't function like an Icon. Why does the timing of Icon creation and icons mostly being in the Hedge matter? What is the actual issue, other than fluff? </div> </div> </div>The actual issue is that Icons are physical metaphors for aspects of specific people and they're mostly only useful with regard to those specific people; your comparison to Promethean doesn't work because, while Vitriol is essentially the physical manifestation of the experiences that produced it (down to losing it resulting in consequences as severe as loss of the attached memories), that's incidental to the things alchemists and Pandorans pursue it for, which is a type of power and energy that Icons don't really have as a generalized quality.<br /> <br /> There's some guidelines in Dark Eras 2's chapter on the Seven Wonders for playing fetches on a Pilgrimage in the unique circumstances that time period offers, if that's your speed, but as it stands I think there's plenty of things you can do to make &quot;there's something going after fetches in general to harvest resources&quot; a viable antagonist hook without involving a very specific other phenomenon.<br /> <br /> You might involve the Hall of Mirrors, or tap into Autumn Nightmares' set of mechanics for changelings harvesting fetch-parts, or invoke a weird inversion of the Gentry's investiture of Titles into Huntsmen in Bastions, depending on what the thrust of the chronicle is \u2014 but playing a fetch is already mechanically very close to playing a mortal and any modification of the game is going to have to account for that in terms of adjustments to both the mechanics and the setting.<br /> <br /> Legitimately, how much interaction do you foresee the characters having with their changeling counterparts versus the fae in general versus The Specific Villain That Is Doing This Thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T06:05:53-08:00","id":1364743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364691#post1364691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, a fetch realizes something is amiss when they start being able to see through the Mask, which coincides with the person whose shadow they have escaping Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, they can see through the Mask well before their counterpart escapes.<br /> <br /> From Attuned to the Wyrd (both editions): &quot;All fetches can recognize changelings for what they are, <b>even before the changeling to whom they are attuned returns to the mortal world</b>.&quot; (emphasis mine). It's the first line of the Echo all Fetches have immediately and automatically. Attuned to the Wyrd doesn't mention if they can also see Hedge gates, tokens, True Fae miens, or even through the masks of other Fetches, but they can clearly tell what a changeling is long before their own personal nemesis appears.<br /> <br /> The book also implies that the Fetch just <i>knows</i> when their changeling is back in the mortal world. From the section on Storytelling The Fetch:<br /> <br /> &quot;What form does the realization take? One fetch sits bolt upright one night, in the middle of a panic attack so intense he can barely breathe. Another finds herself standing in a crowded square one day, tears running down her face, because she suddenly cannot remember her name or where she lives.&quot; Only the last example is of a Fetch who only found out they had a duplicate because they literally faced their counterpart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethean is a game where character advancement is dependent upon Vitriol and hanging onto it in an unspent form is a risk balanced by the drawbacks of raising Azoth. It is a game where the volatility of your occult nature and your lack of a normal human background are things that give you cause to struggle with the question of humanity in a different manner to the placeholder for a person who was, in many cases, literally stolen from their life. The reasons a changeling has for seeking the destruction of their fetch are personal and typically have little to do with the wisps of magic giving it thought and motion. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but killing fetches to regain a piece of themselves is all over the lore of Changeling. That was the whole point of the Broken Mirror Merit in 1e. In 2e, what happens game-system-wise when a changeling kills a Fetch is left more open-ended. The same with mechanical benefits for reclaiming or merging with the Fetch -- and permanently increasing Clarity is explicitly mentioned. Which is what an Icon does. It's not a great leap, then, to just use the Icon rules for the Shadow. It doesn't stop other Icons from existing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The actual issue is that Icons are physical metaphors for aspects of specific people and they're mostly only useful with regard to those specific people; </div> </div> </div>Like, say, a physical metaphor for a soul used in the creation of a being of glamour and sticks, and that killing or merging with this being is thought to improve a changeling's ability to regain their place in the world? The important part of the Shadow being an Icon is that both the fetch and the changeling to which they're bound have reasons for wanting it, and those reasons are mutually exclusive. The fact that other Changelings might have cause for wanting it isn't really important...but the fact that they <i>could</i> harvest a Shadow from a Fetch provides a good reason for Fetch to consider any Changeling they meet a potential existential threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> your comparison to Promethean doesn't work because, while Vitriol is essentially the physical manifestation of the experiences that produced it (down to losing it resulting in consequences as severe as loss of the attached memories), that's incidental to the things alchemists and Pandorans pursue it for, which is a type of power and energy that Icons don't really have as a generalized quality. </div> </div> </div>I feel you are missing the point of the comparison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's some guidelines in Dark Eras 2's chapter on the Seven Wonders for playing fetches on a Pilgrimage in the unique circumstances that time period offers, if that's your speed </div> </div> </div>Good to know, and I might use those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but as it stands I think there's plenty of things you can do to make &quot;there's something going after fetches in general to harvest resources&quot; a viable antagonist hook without involving a very specific other phenomenon. You might involve the Hall of Mirrors, or tap into Autumn Nightmares' set of mechanics for changelings harvesting fetch-parts, or invoke a weird inversion of the Gentry's investiture of Titles into Huntsmen in Bastions, depending on what the thrust of the chronicle is \u2014 but playing a fetch is already mechanically very close to playing a mortal and any modification of the game is going to have to account for that in terms of adjustments to both the mechanics and the setting. </div> </div> </div>He's not harvesting resources, they're essentially trophies that he's deluding himself he's collecting so he can give them back to the people that they came from so they can experience the same rush he did when he murdered his own fetch. He's effectively a fetch serial killer with an elaborate self-justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> invoke a weird inversion of the Gentry's investiture of Titles into Huntsmen in Bastions </div> </div> </div>Like, for instance, a physical manifestation of a memory that serves as the fetch's tie to their counterpart, torn from the person at the time of the abduction and serving as the anchor on which the fetch's personality and very existence rests, which a specific changeling might like to reclaim because it bolsters their ability to tell what is real and what isn't, and which a different changeling might want to get because it would give them deeply personal information on a rival or enemy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Legitimately, how much interaction do you foresee the characters having with their changeling counterparts versus the fae in general versus The Specific Villain That Is Doing This Thing? </div> </div> </div>The Fetch's own changeling counterpart is meant to serve as their primary personal antagonist. The Specific Villain is in a position to gather a bunch of newly-escaped changelings into a motley free of the influence of the greater changeling society -- he's their only source of information on what being a changeling entails, at least for the moment, and he sees them as potential recruits for his Bridge Burning crusade. There's Another Villain around, a True Fae who wants to engineer conflicts between Fetch he created and their counterparts because he believes if his fetch prove themselves &quot;better&quot; than the people they were based on it will fulfill an oath he made and allow him to return to Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T12:04:37-08:00","id":1364804,"title":"","content":"Let me restate my original question:<br /> <br /> Fetches are created in part by taking a piece of the changeling donor's shadow to serve as the basis for their personality and memories, which is often thought of as a metaphor for the soul. The Icon <i>mechanics </i>strike me as a good way to model the effects of a changeling who destroys or merges with their fetch and regaining that piece of soul. There is an added benefit of making the destruction of a fetch other than one's own an attractive possibility to other changelings or other interested parties such as Huntsmen, who could use the shadow <i>as if it were</i> an Icon and gain possibly compromising pre-Durance information and a way to track a specific changeling. This means that any changeling is potentially an enemy to a fetch, which helps up the paranoia factor of their existence (great for generating conflict for drama's sake).<br /> <br /> Is there any good <i>mechanical</i> reason I'd be off base about that? Are there other ways to model this, and, if so, what would they be?<br /> <br /> Also, what mechanical benefits might a Fetch get for having a piece of Shadow. My idea is that it also represents the Jungian Shadow of the original Changeling, and might work the same way a Vice would. But Fetches already get Needles and Threads, so would giving them a third method of regaining Willpower be too much? If so, what other ways could it be used, as the immediate thing that comes to mind is that the Shadow has some effect on a fetch's Integrity, or might be a way of gaining Beats, or as a replacement of Needle or Thread, but I'm unsure how to go about implementing those ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":25851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","user":"TheStray7","date":". 02-02-2020, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T16:30:07-08:00","id":1364868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364804#post1364804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me restate my original question:<br /> <br /> Fetches are created in part by taking a piece of the changeling donor's shadow to serve as the basis for their personality and memories, which is often thought of as a metaphor for the soul. The Icon <i>mechanics </i>strike me as a good way to model the effects of a changeling who destroys or merges with their fetch and regaining that piece of soul. There is an added benefit of making the destruction of a fetch other than one's own an attractive possibility to other changelings or other interested parties such as Huntsmen, who could use the shadow <i>as if it were</i> an Icon and gain possibly compromising pre-Durance information and a way to track a specific changeling. This means that any changeling is potentially an enemy to a fetch, which helps up the paranoia factor of their existence (great for generating conflict for drama's sake).<br /> <br /> Is there any good <i>mechanical</i> reason I'd be off base about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are bound and determined to have the shadow-scrap act exactly like an Icon, nobody is stopping you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there other ways to model this, and, if so, what would they be? </div> </div> </div>Offhand:<br /> <br /> The shadow exerts a strong pull on Icons relating to the changeling's mortal life, such that it's rare not to find at least one squirreled away in the fetch's Bastion, where pulling it free is a substantially difficult act of oneiromancy; killing the fetch releases enough fae energy to shunt an Icon its dreams hold into the relevant changeling (if present) or catalyze the shadow into a Hedge ghost with unerring knowledge of the direction of (and possibly possession of one of) the changeling's mortal Icons (it flees to the Hedge unless captured, and it ceases to exist once the relevant Icons are integrated).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what mechanical benefits might a Fetch get for having a piece of Shadow. My idea is that it also represents the Jungian Shadow of the original Changeling, and might work the same way a Vice would. But Fetches already get Needles and Threads, so would giving them a third method of regaining Willpower be too much? If so, what other ways could it be used, as the immediate thing that comes to mind is that the Shadow has some effect on a fetch's Integrity, or might be a way of gaining Beats, or as a replacement of Needle or Thread, but I'm unsure how to go about implementing those ideas. </div> </div> </div>Offhand:<br /> <br /> <b>New Persistent Condition: Shadowbound</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Once per session, when you would roll for an Integrity breaking point or Clarity attack, instead take the Spooked Condition and regain a number of points of spent Willpower equal to the higher of Wyrd and the highest penalty on the roll.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Be a fetch; Kill a fetch; Have the shadow granted to you through pledgecraft.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Differentiate yourself from the person your changeling used to be, such that their friends and family prefer you as you are or you have one less thing they want; Make a meaningful step in taking over the life of the fetch who previously held the shadow.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Die; Raise your Wyrd above the rating of the fetch who was killed to get the shadow; Forfeit the shadow to someone else via pledgecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T17:38:26-08:00","id":1364884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1360932-looking-for-help-to-make-fetch-splats-for-a-chronicle-idea?p=1364868#post1364868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shadow exerts a strong pull on Icons relating to the changeling's mortal life, such that it's rare not to find at least one squirreled away in the fetch's Bastion, where pulling it free is a substantially difficult act of oneiromancy; killing the fetch releases enough fae energy to shunt an Icon its dreams hold into the relevant changeling (if present) or catalyze the shadow into a Hedge ghost with unerring knowledge of the direction of (and possibly possession of one of) the changeling's mortal Icons (it flees to the Hedge unless captured, and it ceases to exist once the relevant Icons are integrated).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty. I like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>New Persistent Condition: Shadowbound</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Once per session, when you would roll for an Integrity breaking point or Clarity attack, instead take the Spooked Condition and regain a number of points of spent Willpower equal to the higher of Wyrd and the highest penalty on the roll.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Be a fetch; Kill a fetch; Have the shadow granted to you through pledgecraft.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Differentiate yourself from the person your changeling used to be, such that their friends and family prefer you as you are or you have one less thing they want; Make a meaningful step in taking over the life of the fetch who previously held the shadow.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Die; Raise your Wyrd above the rating of the fetch who was killed to get the shadow; Forfeit the shadow to someone else via pledgecraft. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> <br /> As for what the Shadow is doing for the Fetch themselves, this is what I've come up with so far:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When The Gentry take someone, they bind a piece of that person's shadow to the Fetch in order to give them the necessary memories and emotional responses they'll need to believably impersonate the original. This shadow is not just a metaphor for the soul -- it's a portion of the original's archetypal Jungian Shadow, that part of their subconscious which contains those darker emotions they might wish to repress. Thus, a Fetch's Shadow is the emotion that feels most </span></span></span><i>real</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> to them, and acting on it renews the pledge that allows them to act in their original's stead, helps relieve stress, and reinforces their sense of self -- even if it's not healthy behavior in the long run. Whenever a Fetch acts in a manner that takes the easy way out at the expense of their goals or relationships, causing themselves a minor setback in the process, they regain a point of Glamour, and whenever they harvest Glamour from someone experiencing the same emotion they gain an additional point on a successful roll.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Essentially, it acts like a Vice, but regains Glamour instead of Willpower and allows the Fetch to regain additional glamour, similar to how a Changeling's Court Mantle provides extra Glamour when harvesting but also has an act they can perform to regain Glamour without a harvest.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of the Fetch gaining Beats for acting as their own person, rather than a copy of their changeling, however. The Shadow is a Gentry-imposed compulsion; breaking free of that might be something a Fetch would aspire to, especially after discovering the truth about what they are.<br /> <br /> So what about something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>New Persistent Condition</b>: Shadow's Defiance<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your character decides to reject the Gentry-imposed compulsion to act in a manner consistent with the darker impulses of the person they were based on, and attempts to find their own place in the world through their own wants and desires. You cannot regain Glamour from your Shadow, and you do not gain extra Glamour when you harvest your Shadow's emotion from others. You gain no benefits from Allies or Contacts that represent the friends and family from your Changeling's life.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Losing Integrity from meeting your Changeling counterpart or discovering you are an artificial being.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Regain a dot of Integrity, lose <i>another</i> point of Integrity, take meaningful steps to make amends and repair your previous relationships, act in such a manner that your previous friends and family actually prefer you as you are now.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Your character take actions to deliberately differentiate themselves from the person their changeling counterpart used to be, especially if such actions alienate their friends and family.<br /> <br /> Edit: huh. I'm thinking about Shadows on Groundhog's Day...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":25851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","user":"TheStray7","date":". 02-02-2020, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T03:40:24-08:00","id":1365209,"title":"","content":"Do folks have any idea what you'd call a collective group of Fetch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T04:11:04-08:00","id":1365216,"title":"","content":"A posse, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848